Package: thirdreality-gm3server
Version: 0.2.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Depends: libssl3, libmosquitto1
Maintainer: guoping.liu <guoping.liu@3reality.com>
Description: GM3Server - device-side server for ThirdReality LinuxBox (hubv3).
 Pure C server that takes over the server-side role Home Assistant used to play:
 an embedded CivetWeb httpd on :8090 serving the LocalWeb console plus a device
 REST API, a sub-device model fed over MQTT, 14-day history in SQLite, and a
 cloud long-connection with Ed25519 self-attestation. Talks to the local
 mosquitto broker only; the Zigbee and Matter protocol stacks stay in
 zigbee2mqtt and matter2mqtt. The frontend is compiled into the binary, so
 there are no web assets on disk. This build has the libdatachannel P2P path
 left out: LAN access and the cloud long-connection work, WebRTC does not.
